FeatherPad is a lightweight Qt plain-text editor for Linux. It is independent
of any desktop environment and has:

* Drag-and-drop support, including tab detachment and attachment;
* X11 virtual desktop awareness (using tabs on current desktop but opening a
  new window on another);
* An optionally permanent search-bar with a different search entry
  for each tab;
* Instant highlighting of found matches when searching;
* A docked window for text replacement;
* Support for showing line numbers and jumping to a specific line;
* Automatic detection of text encoding as far as possible and optional saving
  with encoding;
* Syntax highlighting for common programming languages;
* Printing;
* Text zooming;
* Appropriate but non-interrupting prompts;

B::Keywords supplies several arrays of exportable keywords: @Scalars, @Arrays,
@Hashes, @Filehandles, @Symbols, @Functions, @Barewords, @TieIOMethods,
@UNIVERSALMethods and @ExporterSymbols.

The @Symbols array includes the contents of each of @Scalars, @Arrays, @Hashes,
@Functions and @Filehandles.

Similarly, @Barewords adds a few non-function keywords and operators to the
@Functions array.

IDLE is Python’s Integrated Development and Learning Environment.

IDLE has the following features: Python shell window (interactive
interpreter) with colorizing of code input, output, and error messages;
multi-window text editor with multiple undo, Python colorizing,
smart indent, call tips, auto completion, and other features;
search within any window, replace within editor windows, and
search through multiple files (grep); debugger with persistent
breakpoints, stepping, and viewing of global and local namespaces;
configuration, browsers, and other dialogs.
